{"id":"74a14febec80f6cb92ed32f0bffa293c9805bbe13182255cb863a0451cd3b298","pubkey":"3d2ebbd741c634fec425ababde63dc1a4387a2fa97f7eea94f3ea7227f19b119","created_at":1782387087,"content":"めも\nhttps://x.com/fashionpressnet/status/2069986462343532927","tags":[]}
{"id":"993c99e10cf5447a36d5ce3031e7034185477221cf65b6c53fcf51f7c36f29ff","pubkey":"16d114303d8203115918ca34a220e925c022c09168175a5ace5e9f3b61640947","created_at":1782386884,"content":"https://npub1zmg3gvpasgp3zkgceg62yg8fyhqz9sy3dqt45kkwt60nkctyp9rs9wyppc.blossom.band/ff4583f49aeea275ef028ec1239f38e2e81652272a03c2dfa918383589aca426.jpg\nThe real test of entrepreneurship is not whether you can survive a grant round, a procurement panel, a tax offset, or a government-backed market.\n\nThe real test is simpler:\n\nIf the state disappeared tomorrow, would your business still have customers?\n\nAustralia is full of “entrepreneurship” that is really just compliance surfing: chase the program, decode the paperwork, satisfy the panel, invoice the department, survive the BAS cycle, then pretend this is market discovery.\n\nMeanwhile, the actual small operator is carrying wages, super, ASIC fees, rent, tax debt, late invoices, and a customer base getting squeezed from every direction.\n\nThat is the down-under comedy:\nthe state calls it innovation, then makes the founder spend half his life proving he is allowed to operate.\n\nAustralia had about 2.73 million actively trading businesses at 30 June 2025, but fewer than 1 million were employing businesses. In 2024–25, there were 437,150 business entries and 370,500 exits — a country full of people having a crack, and a system very good at chewing them up. \n\nCommonwealth procurement is also massive: in 2024–25, reported Australian Government procurement was about $104.9 billion, while SMEs received 45,556 contracts and around $14.7 billion in contract value below the $1 billion threshold. That is opportunity, yes — but also a reminder that plenty of “business” is downstream of Canberra’s tap. \n\nThe cost side keeps rising too: from 1 July 2025 the minimum wage rose to $24.95/hour, super guarantee rose to 12%, and ASIC company registration and review fees increased. None of those are automatically wrong — but they are real weight on anyone trying to employ people honestly. \n\nThen comes the hard scoreboard: ASIC reported 13,413 companies entering external administration in the financial year to 31 May 2025, up 34.2% on the same period the year before.  The RBA also noted that tax liabilities among insolvent firms have risen sharply, with collectable debt from insolvent small businesses more than doubling compared with pre-pandemic levels. \n\nSo the real question is not “are you an entrepreneur?”\n\nThe real question is:\n\nAre you building a business, or are you building a dependency with an ABN?\n\nBecause if the government disappeared tomorrow, the grant-chasers vanish first.\nThe invoice-farm consultants vanish second.\nThe compliance tourists vanish third.\n\nBut the real operator?\nThe one with customers, tools, receipts, reputation, and delivery?\n\nThat one keeps working.\n\n#Entrepreneurship #Australia #SmallBusiness #DownUnder #FounderLife #BusinessReality #StateDependency #ReceiptsNotVibes #Cashflow #BuildOrBeg","tags":[["alt","A short note: https://npub1zmg3gvpasgp3zkgceg62yg8fyhqz9sy3dqt45..."],["t","Entrepreneurship"],["t","entrepreneurship"],["t","Australia"],["t","australia"],["t","SmallBusiness"],["t","smallbusiness"],["t","DownUnder"],["t","downunder"],["t","FounderLife"],["t","founderlife"],["t","BusinessReality"],["t","businessreality"],["t","StateDependency"],["t","statedependency"],["t","ReceiptsNotVibes"],["t","receiptsnotvibes"],["t","Cashflow"],["t","cashflow"],["t","BuildOrBeg"],["t","buildorbeg"],["r","https://npub1zmg3gvpasgp3zkgceg62yg8fyhqz9sy3dqt45kkwt60nkctyp9rs9wyppc.blossom.band/ff4583f49aeea275ef028ec1239f38e2e81652272a03c2dfa918383589aca426.jpg"],["p","16d114303d8203115918ca34a220e925c022c09168175a5ace5e9f3b61640947"],["imeta","url https://npub1zmg3gvpasgp3zkgceg62yg8fyhqz9sy3dqt45kkwt60nkctyp9rs9wyppc.blossom.band/ff4583f49aeea275ef028ec1239f38e2e81652272a03c2dfa918383589aca426.jpg","x ff4583f49aeea275ef028ec1239f38e2e81652272a03c2dfa918383589aca426","size 305208","m image/jpeg","dim 1024x1536","blurhash ^KNAFqt7XAWX-oog.8IoxZoyWBRk00t7s-bIWXs:xuM{bcaxoJt6yFIUxts:bIR*%M%LjXf6WYoJo~IUkDs.jYofR4xZM}ogayju~q-;ROjuWDWB","ox ff4583f49aeea275ef028ec1239f38e2e81652272a03c2dfa918383589aca426"],["client","Amethyst"]]}
